<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  acu bootstrap customization package template - full company contract
  (SPEC T81 single full-company line; T145 bumps 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0 for Role/User;
  T150 bumps 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 for NumberingSequence;
  T154/T155 bumps 1.2.0 -> 1.3.0 for *Preferences field depth, gh #26 / V41).

  package_zip() (bootstrap.py) prefers data-repo bootstrap/project.xml when
  present; otherwise this packaged template is the fallback so config init,
  offline tests, and package-only installs still bootstrap the full surface.

  package_zip() injects a
  <Graph ClassName="AcuBootstrapPlugin" FileType="NewFile" Source="..."/>
  item carrying bootstrap_plugin.cs - the CustomizationPlugin that enables
  features on publish (CS100000 is un-writable through the contract API;
  T3 verdict). Item shape verified vs 26.101.0225: Customization.CstCodeFile
  Tag=Graph, source rides in the Source ATTRIBUTE (XML-escaped), not CDATA.

  Root element shape verified vs the training packages shipped on the live
  box (HelpAndTraining/T*/PhoneRepairShop.zip, same 26.101.0225 build):
  project.xml's root is <Customization level description product-version>;
  the project NAME comes from the import call, not the XML.

  The <EntityEndpoint> item (T12, verified vs 26.101.0225 by import
  round-trip 2026-07-08): the <Endpoint> child is the XmlSerializer form of
  PX.Api.ContractBased.Common.Model.Endpoint - namespace
  http://www.acumatica.com/entity/maintenance/5.31, systemContractVersion 4.

  Full company entity payload (finance + distribution setup surface):
  Company, CreditTerms, Currency, LedgerCompany, FinancialYearSettings,
  MasterCalendar, CompanyCalendar, CompanyPeriod, ManagePeriods,
  GLPreferences, INPreferences, ReasonCode, AP/AR/SO/PO/CA Preferences,
  AvailabilityCalculationRule, PostingClass, VendorClass, StatementCycle,
  Warehouse, OrderType, CashAccount, Role, User (+ UserRole membership detail),
  NumberingSequence.

  T145 Role/User (gh #24) - Default endpoint has no Role/User surface:
  - Role SM201005 -> RoleAccess, PrimaryView Roles (PX.SM.Roles):
    key Rolename; Descr for display. Package template 90-roles seeds the
    full pre-build CompanyID=1 role set (system + module roles from live
    dump) so apply/diff matches a virgin tenant role surface.
  - User SM201010 -> Access, PrimaryView UserList (PX.SM.Users): key
    Username; identity FirstName/LastName/Email + IsApproved +
    PasswordNeverExpires + PasswordChangeOnNextLogin; Password write-only
    (extract/diff policy = V39/T147).
  - membership = User detail Roles -> AllowedRoles (UsersInRoles/Roles
    projection): Rolename + Selected (assign when true). Apply order
    Role then User (V22 prefixes; T148).

  T150 NumberingSequence (gh #25) - Default endpoint has no numbering
  surface; CS201010 Numbering Sequences (NumberingSequenceMaint):
  - PrimaryView Sequence (DAC Numbering): key NumberingID + Descr.
  - Detail view SequenceDetail (DAC NumberingSequence): bounds StartNbr,
    EndNbr, WarnNbr, NbrStep, StartDate. LastNbr is runtime counter —
    omitted from contract (V40/T152 strip/ignore if ever present).
  - Flat entity (Currency multi-view idiom): NumberingID/Descr on Sequence,
    bounds on SequenceDetail. Single sequence row per NumberingID is the
    demo/LAB5 shape; multi-segment / branch-scoped rows are out of v1.

  T154/T155 prefs-field-depth (gh #26 / V41) - curated *Preferences
  deepen from LAB5 inventory *Setup vs virgin ERP defaults. NOT full DAC.
  Each added field has a seed/catalog reason (demo need or rebuild risk).
  Skipped: lot-class / default-site FKs (need apply reorder vs warehouse
  / lot class), CA transfer/register numbering (sequences not packaged),
  server-derived/runtime (B11), aging/retainage/print flags.
  *NumberingID only when package 05-numbering-sequences has the id (V40).
  Pick list (added beyond pre-1.3.0 surface):
  - GLPreferences (GL102000 / GLSetupRecord): +BatchNumberingID (BATCH),
    +AutoPostOption, +HoldEntry, +RequireControlTotal
    (keep YtdNetIncAccountID + RetEarnAccountID)
  - INPreferences (IN101000 / setup): +Batch/Receipt/Issue/Adjustment/
    KitAssembly NumberingID; +AutoPost +SummPost +NegQty
    +RequireControlTotal (keep transit/progress/reason/UpdateGL/HoldEntry)
  - APPreferences (AP101000 / Setup): +Batch/Invoice/Check NumberingID;
    +AutoPost +RequireControlTotal +RequireVendorRef
    +RequireApprovePayments (keep HoldEntry)
  - ARPreferences (AR101000 / ARSetupRecord): +Batch/Invoice/Payment
    NumberingID; +AutoPost +RequireControlTotal +RequireExtRef
    +CreditCheckError (keep HoldEntry)
  - SOPreferences (SO101000 / sosetup): +ShipmentNumberingID
    +CreditCheckError (keep DefaultOrderType/HoldShipments/
    RequireShipmentTotal/AutoReleaseIN)
  - POPreferences (PO101000 / Setup): +RegularPONumberingID
    +ReceiptNumberingID +AutoReleaseAP (keep HoldReceipts/
    RCReturnReasonCodeID/AutoReleaseIN)
  - CAPreferences (CA101000 / CASetupRecord): +BatchNumberingID
    +AutoPostOption +ReleaseAP +ReleaseAR (keep HoldEntry/Transit*)

  Contract field names = DAC property names verbatim (no rename layer).
  Features (CS100000) stays OUT of the endpoint - the plugin owns features.
  Shape change requires a version bump (V21).
-->
